    <div class=3D"s-prose js-post-body" itemprop=3D"text">
<p>If <code>some-boring-process</code> is running in your current bash sess=
ion:</p>

<ol>
<li>halt it with <code>ctrl-z</code> to give you the bash prompt</li>
<li>put it in the background with <code>bg</code></li>
<li>note the job number, or use the <code>jobs</code> command</li>
<li>detach the process from this bash session with <code>disown -h %1</code=
> (substitute the actual job number there).</li>
</ol>

<p>That doesn't do anything to redirect the output -- you have to think of =
that when you launch your boring process. [Edit] There seems to be a way to=
 redirect it <a href=3D"https://gist.github.com/782263" rel=3D"nofollow nor=
eferrer">https://gist.github.com/782263</a></p>

<p>But seriously, look into screen. I have shells on a remote server that h=
ave been running for months.</p>

<hr>

<p>Looks like this:</p>

<pre class=3D"lang-bsh s-code-block"><code data-highlighted=3D"yes" class=
=3D"hljs language-bash">$ <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">sleep</span> 999999
^Z
[1]+  Stopped                 <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">sleep</span> 99=
9999
$ <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">bg</span>
[1]+ <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">sleep</span> 999999 &amp;
$ <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">disown</span> -h %1
</code></pre>
    </div>
