    <div class=3D"s-prose js-post-body" itemprop=3D"text">
<p>If I fire something up which I want to finish no matter what (short of s=
ystem reboot), I use <code>nohup</code> and run it in the background.  Unli=
ke screen and the like you can't reattach to the processs. However, baring =
redirection elsewhere any output can be found in <code>nohup.out</code>. </=
p>

<p>I do use <code>screen</code> when I want to be able to switch terminals =
for a process. Such as starting a process from home/work and switching to t=
he other.  Like any other terminal session output will eventual scroll off =
the top of the buffer.</p>

<p>EDIT: If you have already launched the process, you can <code>disown</co=
de> the process to prevent the <code>HUP</code> signal from being sent when=
 the process closes. </p>
